# ungoogled-chromium / ungoogled-chromium-windows patches that Plain Browser does NOT apply.
# One entry per line, with a prefix:
#   uc:<patch>    ungoogled-chromium/patches/<patch>          ucw:<patch>  ungoogled-chromium-windows/patches/<patch>
#   prune:<file>  a Chromium file that ungoogled's pruning.list deletes and we need
#   hunks:uc:<patch>:<regex>  only the hunks of that upstream patch whose changed lines match <regex>
#                 (scripts/patchfilter.py); the rest of the patch stays applied
# prepare.py drops the patches from the upstream series and the files from pruning.list before a fresh build;
# apply-plainbrowser.ps1 reverses the patches (patch -R, last applied first) and restores the files (git checkout,
# or a download from chromium.googlesource.com) on an already-built tree; check-patches.py skips the patches' hunks.
#
# Safe Browsing: ungoogled compiles it out (safe_browsing_mode=0, hard-coded in buildflags.gni by the Windows
# patch) and deletes the code that depends on it. Plain Browser keeps Safe Browsing (local hash database through
# our proxy, patches/70-safebrowsing) and keeps ungoogled's two iridium patches that disable incident reporting
# and extended reporting.
ucw:ungoogled-chromium/windows/windows-fix-building-without-safebrowsing.patch
uc:core/ungoogled-chromium/fix-building-without-safebrowsing.patch
uc:core/inox-patchset/0001-fix-building-without-safebrowsing.patch
# Pruned files Safe Browsing needs back (prefs and the default download file-type policy):
prune:components/safe_browsing/core/common/safe_browsing_prefs.cc
prune:components/safe_browsing/core/common/safe_browsing_prefs.h
prune:components/safe_browsing/content/resources/empty_file_type_policy.pb
# ungoogled removes the Safe Browsing preferences (registration, policy handlers, settings UI bindings, users)
# together with other unused prefs in one patch. Only its Safe Browsing hunks are dropped; the rest stays.
hunks:uc:core/ungoogled-chromium/remove-unused-preferences-fields.patch:safe_browsing|SafeBrowsing|safebrowsing
